I might point out too that simply because the qualifier has instructed
the compiler to use/generate 64 bit pointers does not imply that one is
able to access the 64 bit address space on VMS.


__int64 x(__int64 **p) { return **p; }

32 bit:   Alpha              
          ===================
   ==>    LDL     R16, (R16)	; implicit sign extension
          LDQ     R0, (R16)
          RET     R26

          Itanium
          ===================
   ==>    ld4     r32 = [r32]   
          sxt4    r32 = r32     ; explicit sign extension
          ld8     r8 = [r32]                       
          br.ret.sptk.many rp


64 bit:   Alpha              
          ===================
   ==>    LDQ     R16, (R16)                             
          LDQ     R0, (R16)
          RET     R26                                    

          Itanium
          ===================
   ==>    ld8     r32 = [r32]                      
          ld8     r8 = [r32]                       
          br.ret.sptk.many rp

All addressing is 64 bits!
