Absolutely should not be necessary. Have a look in your /usr/lib/gcc 
directory, e.g.

ldo@theon:~> ls -ld /usr/lib/gcc/*/
drwxr-xr-x 5 root root 4096 Aug 21 13:25 /usr/lib/gcc/x86_64-linux-gnu/

There should be one of these subdirectories for each architecture that your 
GCC can (cross-)compile to, containing architecture-specific libraries and 
include files.

Cross-compilation is an integral part of the way GCC is designed.


