I don't remember 64 bit or not, but I do remember that VMS was
available before OSF/1.  In 1994 we had an Alpha, and
we were supposed to run VMS on it, as OSF/1 wasn't ready.  
That was a big deal, as the supply of DECNet addresses was limited.
But then OSF/1 came out just in time, and we didn't need the
DECNet address after all.

We also had Ultrix machines, and would have used one as a gateway
between TCP/IP and DECNet.  That would mean late 1994 for OSF/1.

I don't remember anything about 64 bit addressing, it was the 64 bit
data size that was useful at the time.  

-- glen


