Like I said, YOU didn't make the transition.  Now, do you need full 64 bits?
If you're just playing about in normal process space, you've no need for it.
P0/P1 addresses extend to 00000000.xxxxxxxx and S0/S1 to FFFFFFFF.xxxxxxxx.

If you _require_ 64 bit addressing within portions of the code, you can use:

#pragma required_pointer_size save
#pragma required_pointer_size long

  <your 64 bit code>

#pragma required_pointer_size restore

In some cases, going to the 64 bit pointer will save you and instruction or
three due to implicit sign-extention operations but it's not really a great
big savings on CPU performance unless you're doing it a gazillion times.

