Well that is true, but for high performance number crunching, you
really can't do much swapping.   If you include the memory used
by the OS, 32 bits was enough for at least 4GB physical for 
real problems.

Also, even though many systems had
64 bit floating point, if the memory path was 8 or 16 bits, it would
be pretty slow.  (That is, 8087 with 8088 or 8086 or 80287 with
80286 or 80386.)

-- glen


