VMS users generally had application compatibility at source level
(that was the VMS way from day one) and at binary level not just
across different processors within an architecture but even when
transitioning between processor architectures. For the transition that
mattered, VAX to Alpha, binary translators - not emulators - were
available e.g. for folks who may not have had access to application
sources. Some restrictions exist, terms and conditions apply, etc.
Whether the licence Ts+Cs of a particular DEC or 3rd party licence
permitted transferring the software without a matching licence
transfer is a discussion not directly related to what software
technology is available and works.


