-taso ("truncated address space option") was a compile+link option
used on DEC OSF/1 to aid porting broken C applications from 32bit Unix
to 64bit Unix, by trying to ensure that a valid pointer could be
stored in an int, with some expectation of being able to do something
useful with it later.

