> mattered, VAX to Alpha, binary translators - not emulators - were
> available e.g. for folks who may not have had access to application
> sources. Some restrictions exist, terms and conditions apply, etc.

Binary translators also exist from Alpha to Itanium. In both cases, you 
obviously don't get the same performance as from a recompile/relink, but 
you get the same application results as on the platform you are 
replacing (compared to getting stuck without the sources available on 
"modern" non-propriatary systems).

Hans.


