Reminds me of what IBM did to get MVS to run on 64 bit machines.

So many control blocks allow for 31 (or even 24) bit addresses
and can't be extended.  Executable code can only be in addresses
reachable in 31 bits.  A DCB must be in the low 16M, to be
addressable in 24 bits.

