I just ran a C program on gein.vistech.net (Alpha OpenVMS 7.3.1, I believe) 
containing the following line

    fprintf(stdout, "sizeof(void *) = %d\n", sizeof(void *));

and was surprised to see it print out

    sizeof(void *) = 4

So OpenVMS never made the transition to a full 64-bit OS!? Which means the 
only 64-bit OS from DEC was OSF/1 1.2 released March 1993 
<http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tru64_UNIX>. And the only other 64-bit OS for 
Alpha was Linux, ported the following year.


