Without the ckt diagram in front of me, I cannot make specific
suggestions.
In general, your thinking of replacing associated parts is correct.  A
new flyback may produce more electrical stress on degraded components
which would cause them to fail soon after the flyback is installed.

I would replace the following:
1) horizontal output transistor (try to get the exact replacement
part.  If not possible, a sub from NTE or equivalent will most likely
work)
2) the capacitors on the input side of the flyback xformer (get the
exact mfd rating, higher WVDC and temp coeff is desirable, but not
necessary)
3) the capacitors on the output side of the flyback (get the exact mfd
rating, higher WVDC and temp coeff is desirable, but not necessary)
4) diodes and the high voltage rectifiers on the output of the
flyback.
Make sure  solder joints are well done, rounded if possible, and
excess flux is removed.
Carefully inspect ckt board traces in this area for microscopic
breaks, dress with solder as appropriate.

Good luck!
John


